=== Changelog ===

==== Unreleased ====
* Releases: every install kit (RA kits included), the VARIANTS and DEBUG zips and the standalone loader downloads (on GitHub and on the MEGA mirror) now carry LICENSE-LIBSMB2.txt, the LGPL-2.1 licence of Ronnie Sahlberg (https://github.com/sahlberg)'s libsmb2 (https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2) that every loader embeds for SMB2 browsing. The bug-report zip already carries the same licence text, under licenses/libsmb2/. Packaging only; the loader is unchanged.
* Releases: a rolling release now carries RIPTOPL-BUGREPORT-<version>.zip, a bug-report build, whenever its diagnostics build succeeded (best-effort: if neither toolchain produced one, the run shows a warning and the release ships without it): the OPLDIAG build (start-up steps on screen, stage colours, freeze and crash reports on the memory card) left uncompressed, so it keeps the layout of a standard ps2sdk link, with a README on how to use it and what to send (photo, RIPTOPL-FREEZE.TXT / RIPTOPL-CRASH.TXT, DIAG.TXT). Built by the official container, else by ps2dev:latest; the publisher refuses a packed or padded loader. Requested by Volventura. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* SMB2 is back on OPL's own core: Settings > Network > SMB Version (SMBv1 default, or SMB2) now works again, for browsing and in game. Browsing uses a new smb2man driver over Ronnie Sahlberg (https://github.com/sahlberg)'s libsmb2 (https://github.com/sahlberg/libsmb2, vendored at c6e4997, LGPL-2.1); games read through a new SMB2 build of the in-game module (SMB 2.0.2 and 2.1, NTLMv2 logon, signing when the server requires it, guest and anonymous logons). SMBv1 is unchanged and stays the default; if the SMB2 driver cannot load, browsing falls back to SMBv1, and a game always uses the dialect the menu is browsing with. SMB 3.x is not offered. Changing the version while an SMB driver is loaded offers a restart. Host-tested against Samba; NOT TESTED on hardware, PCSX2 or a Windows server.
* Interface: new Boot Theme Wait setting (Settings > Interface, under Alternate Background). It is how many seconds the start-up screen waits for your saved theme while the drive that holds it is still starting up (0 to 10). It is Off by default, so the menu opens right away and the saved theme replaces the built-in one as soon as its drive is up. Before, the start-up screen always waited up to 6 s, which every boot paid in full when the saved theme was no longer there. Set it to 6 for the old behaviour. Saved as boot_theme_wait. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Start-up: a settings file that does not exist is now opened once instead of twice (each settings name has several fallback names, and on an MMCE every failed open is a round trip over SIO2), and DIAG.TXT now times each step of the settings load, the boot device start-up and the intro (including how long it waited for the saved theme and the boot sound). From Volventura's report of a slow start-up from mmce0. Tandem of the RiptOPL change. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Video modes: three new flicker-filtered HIRES modes at the end of the Video Mode list: PAL 704x576i (HIRES, FLICKER FILTER), NTSC 704x480i (HIRES, FLICKER FILTER) and NTSC 704x480i (HIRES, 448 lines, FLICKER FILTER). They are the same as the existing HIRES modes (same sharpness, same 4:3 safe area), but the GS shows every line mixed half-and-half with the line below it, so thin lines and text edges no longer flicker between the two interlaced fields. The FLICKER-FREE 640-wide modes are unchanged. Reported by zackcage6 (https://github.com/zackcage6) in RiptOPL #132. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Robustness fixes from YAOPL (https://github.com/yaopl/yaopl): HD Pro releases its transfer lock when a DMA transfer fails to start or finish, and clears its busy flag on every attempt, so one failed transfer no longer blocks every later one. The PNG loader keeps its palette per load instead of one shared by the menu and the art loader, and refuses images larger than 1024 x 1024. The app menu returns to the main screen instead of drawing or acting on a menu that failed to allocate, or on a row that a list reread removed. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL 639934b, 2380267 and c6fc06f (Roman Kelesidis, https://github.com/belomaxorka). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Controllers: pressing a DualShock's ANALOG button no longer stalls menu scrolling. The menu now checks that the pad accepted its analog-mode lock and sends the lock again, in a quiet moment, when a reconnect or a refused request left the pad unlocked (at most three tries per pad). An unlocked pad identifies itself again on every ANALOG press and reports nothing for about a quarter of a second, so pressing ANALOG repeatedly paused scrolling for seconds. Reported by zackcage6 (https://github.com/zackcage6) in RiptOPL #133 and Open-PS2-Loader #1106. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* MX4SIO: partial multi-sector reads and writes retry from the next untransferred sector, with the remaining write count. Builds embed a local driver with PS2HomeDeveloper's ps2sdk #936 correction instead of the SDK IRX; VMC erases can use four-sector batches again. Host fault-injection and target driver builds passed; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Neutrino over SMB (experimental): a game on the Neutrino core (its own Loader Core, or Default while the global Loader Core is Neutrino) now launches from SMB through Neutrino's new SMB backend (-bsd=smb), from Ronnie Sahlberg (https://github.com/sahlberg)'s ps2max32/neutrino PR #236 (https://github.com/ps2max32/neutrino/pull/236, merged as 1bff25bcfa02e192f5b35cadbe53648786813974; install the complete latest nightly) on his usmb2 client (https://github.com/sahlberg/usmb2). The menu's network and share settings are written into the Neutrino folder's config/bsd-smb.toml before launch. Default follows the global Loader Core, in favourites and the core-aware menus too, and a per-game OPL or Neutrino choice still wins. A share not on port 445, a game with a VMC, or a Neutrino without the SMB modules falls back to the OPL core with a warning. The share must speak SMB 3.0 (for PS2-Servers, its SMBv3 card on port 445). See docs/NEUTRINO.md. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* VMC: in-game saves on a BDM VMC (USB, iLink, internal ATA, UDPBD) erase each block in 4-sector writes instead of 16 single ones, reducing device-write calls; MX4SIO now uses the same batches with the driver fix in the MX4SIO entry above (ps2dev/ps2sdk#936). The VMC dialog now says under the card name whether it is the game's series card, its own card or a generic card. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Compatibility defaults: Jak and Daxter: The Precursor Legacy (SCUS_971.24, SCES_503.61, SCES_506.14, SCPS_150.21, SCPS_550.04) defaults to Unhook Syscalls and Disable IGR on the OPL core, to address the reported "Sony presents" hang (upstream OPL #1171). A game that already has saved compatibility modes keeps them. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Boot: no endless waits before the first frame. After 10 s with no pad port opened the boot splash is drawn and the wait logged instead of a black screen, the ds34usb/ds34bt binds give up after 3 s, and START (safe boot) skips the optional fallback-font probe. Diagnostic builds mark seven boot stages, each with its own limit (20 s, or 60 s for the intro stage), show the stalled stage's colour before the usual report colours, and list how far the boot got in the freeze report. Reported as a black screen before the menu on a SCPH-30005R. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* CDVDMAN: while a stream is open, a game's own read now finishes on the game's callback instead of the stream's, and a held-off stream fill restarts after it. This addresses callback routing investigated for the Tales of the Abyss field freeze (RiptOPL #185); the freeze is not confirmed fixed. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Video modes: PAL 704x576i and NTSC 704x480i (HIRES) now draw the menu inside a 4:3 safe area instead of across the whole picture, leaving the same margins as the standard 640-wide modes, so a 4:3 CRT should no longer cut it off at the left and right (and, on PAL, the top and bottom). The menu takes the same width as the standard 640-wide modes (1:1, so art is no longer stretched 10% sideways), 480 lines on NTSC (1:1) and 512 lines on PAL (as 640x512i); Overscan shrinks it further as before. A new last Video Mode, NTSC 704x480i @60Hz 24bit (HIRES, 448 lines), keeps the menu in the 640x448 area of 640x448i for a CRT that still hides the top or bottom of the 480-line one, since NTSC 704x480i uses every line at Overscan 0 (Overscan shrinks the menu area and V-POS moves it, which also help there). 704x480p, 704x576p, 720p and 1080i are unchanged. Reported by zackcage6 (https://github.com/zackcage6) in RiptOPL #132. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* USB controllers: the ShanWan PS3 clone pad (USB ID 2563:0575) now works in the menu and in games (ds34usb.irx and usb_pademu.irx). It is no longer sent the DS3 enable, LED/rumble or pairing-address reports, which it does not answer, and its plain HID report is read as it is. A pad interface that reports no endpoints is refused, and the menu driver no longer reads a stale buffer when the first report times out. Ported from freergam3r's findings in [Fgr-35/Modified-drivers-for-usb-controller-in-opl](https://github.com/Fgr-35/Modified-drivers-for-usb-controller-in-opl). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Drawing: 1-2 pixel separators, borders and PSBBN Flow stars no longer vanish on 224 to 448 line screens, and after a slow frame the picture flips on the next real VSync instead of mid-scanout. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Themes: an alternate background in the same conf_theme.cfg. alt= beside an element's default= (or once at the top level for every Background element) names a second picture, shown while the new Settings > Interface > Alternate Background is on (default Off, saved as theme_alt_bg). Themes without alt= look the same either way and are not reloaded when the setting changes; alt_hd=/alt_sd= work as for any key. Idea: KrahJohlito (https://github.com/KrahJohlito). Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Settings dialogs: long labels wrap, other labels and values that do not fit end in "...", the keyboard editor's title fits, and the About page's coder rows are rebalanced, so no text draws past the screen edge. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* File Manager: Start > File Manager browses every started drive (BDM drives, MMCE, memory cards, the loader's own APA partition, UDPFS and SMB) and copies, moves, renames and deletes files without booting another program. Square marks, Triangle shows the actions, L1/R1 turn pages and Circle goes up a folder; an .elf can be run, a .psu unpacked, and save folders pasted as .psu backups. See docs/FILE_MANAGER.md. VMC Saves can also copy a save out as a .psu and copy a .psu in (see docs/VMC.md). Background music now plays Ogg streams whose serial number has its top bit set. All three from akilluminati47's RIPPS2 (https://github.com/akilluminati47/RIPPS2, builds 51 and 91 to 125). Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Theme View switch: changing the view (Settings > Interface > Theme View, or holding L3) no longer corrupts memory and crashes on a later switch. Each game row's cover slots now follow the theme on screen: rows built for another theme load are reset, and grown when the new view has more cover caches (Grid has a back-cover cache per block), so a cover can also no longer show another game's art. Reported in RiptOPL #211. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Settings: a failed settings-home recovery no longer loses sets it had already read. When the boot home lacks some of them (conf_game.cfg, network, apps), they are taken from the legacy home that has them, such as mc0:/OPL on an mc0:/APPS boot, and every set then points back at the boot home; files in the boot home always win. A deferred network boot that keeps its home on the memory card now applies its conf_network.cfg. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Message screens: long text on the warning screen, the text screens, the video-mode confirmation and the Remove Settings prompt now wraps inside the screen's frame and is centred line by line, instead of running off the screen as one line (long translations did). Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL 6a091fc (Roman Kelesidis). Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Background Art and the boot theme hold, follow-ups: Coverflow keeps the last background while it defers its request, a page with no games drops the kept one, and the boot hold keeps the menu's update hook running so a theme drive that comes up late is still seen. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Settings: RiptOPL no longer reads official OPL's conf_opl.cfg as a read-only starting point. With no RiptOPL settings in its home it starts from its defaults; its own settings_riptopl.cfg, an older conf_riptopl.cfg and settings carried over from an APA home still load. When the known settings home misses, its other files (conf_game.cfg, network, last played, apps) are now re-read instead of dropped, so a first run beside official OPL's files keeps its global game settings. See docs/AUTOLAUNCH-GLOBAL-SETTINGS.md. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* .hack//Infection (SLUS_202.67, SLES_522.37, SLKA_250.80) on the OPL core: its IOP allocations get pads, like Neutrino's Mode 7. The three blocks the game overruns (neutrino #92) get the overrun plus 256 bytes and every other block 256 bytes; fixed-address requests stay unpadded, and a padded block that does not fit falls back to its normal size. The FREEZEDIAG flavour also writes an IOP heap freeze report. Reported by Ethyls. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Grid view: RIPPS2's grid in full, from akilluminati47 (RIPGRID, builds 78 to 117). Whole pages that stay still while the cursor moves and turn as a whole; L1/R1 turn a page and keep the cursor's place (they do not wrap when every cover fits on one page); the selected cover is drawn 12% larger inside breathing rings; the built-in Grid shows 4 x 2 covers (6 x 2 on 16:9). Left from the first column opens a device sidebar (Up/Down switch device), a new page slides in at Coverflow's Animation Speed, holding the right stick to one side turns the selected case to its back cover (COV2), covers not selected get a vignette, and a game with no art gets a tile with its name or serial. Settings > Interface > Coverflow Settings > Grid Layout picks Theme, 4 x 2, 5 x 2, 3 x 2 Large or 6 x 3 Compact. New theme keys <block>_counter, _title, _devices, _flip, _vignette and _coverless. See docs/THEME_ENGINE.md and docs/CONTROLS.md. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Theme View lists Coverflow (3) and Coverflow (5) as two entries, and holding L3 steps through List, Coverflow (3), Coverflow (5), PSBBN Flow and Grid. Settings keep theme_view=coverflow plus coverflow_count, so older configurations load the same count; the Cover Count row leaves Coverflow Settings. A new Library row right under Theme View picks Pages or All Games List (the same all_games setting as Game Sources). Idea: KrahJohlito. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* All Games list: device tabs whose games are on it step aside, and so does the Apps tab once the apps are on it; a device that is pulled out or switched Off leaves the list, a switched-off BDM transport stays out when it reappears, and the page draws no page icon. See docs/GAME-LIBRARY.md. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Background music: a stream that decodes no audio (64 reads in a row with no PCM) now stops the music instead of spinning the GUI's priority; a player that stopped on its own is released before the next start, and an aborted prebuffer lets the music start again. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Diagnostic builds (OPLDIAG=1): a watchdog reports a menu that stops drawing. When no frame finishes for 8 s (20 s while booting) the screen turns magenta and mc0:/RIPTOPL-FREEZE.TXT (mc1: as a fallback) gets the GUI frame step, every EE thread's state and wait, the pad fault counters and the diag log; the screen then turns green, or orange when no card took the file. Other builds compile it away. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* RetroAchievements: View achievements no longer tries to save RA/<game ID>.ach (the In-Game Menu's Left To Hunt list) on a read-only device. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Releases: the version is now the last part of every release ZIP name, the source snapshot and the Korium channel's archives included. The rolling-ra channel's date now refreshes on every publish.
* Controllers: one press no longer moves the cursor twice. A pad that answers no read for a moment (while it takes a rumble alignment or the ANALOG button) keeps what it last reported for up to 300 ms instead of reading as released, and rumble is aligned only while the pad is quiet (RIPPS2's gate, akilluminati47). Found with zackcage6's RIPTOPL-NAVTRACE capture. Host-tested on the recorded trace; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Video modes: after a 704-wide, 720p or 1080i menu mode, the GUI thread gets its priority back, so it no longer sits above the background-music threads until reboot. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* PS1 covers no longer flicker between their art and the placeholder on a full art cache (Coverflow warming): a row on its name art stays on it. Reported by Davood TiTaN. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* About page: the title shows the whole version and the build options line is no longer cut at 39 characters (both were formatted into 40-byte buffers). NathanNeurotic is credited among the coders; Network update now shares one row with its name so the dialog keeps its height. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL 9847f4ca (Roman Kelesidis). PS2SDK build passed; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Themes: an AttributeImage and a game-art image (GameImage, Background) never share an image cache, even when the attribute and the pattern have the same name. Sharing one made the game image index cache_id[-1] and look for its art in the theme folder. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL cc3d59f0 (Roman Kelesidis). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Colours: a text colour change now reaches the info, apps, Favourites and PS1 screens too, not only the main list; elements whose colour the theme sets, and images, keep theirs. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL d21b3bc5 (Roman Kelesidis). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Background Art: while the selected game's background is still loading, the last one stays on screen instead of flashing to the default picture on every step; a game known to have no background shows the default as before. No extra memory (BG caches already keep 2 pictures). Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL 2bc4d161 (Roman Kelesidis). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Boot: when the saved theme is a disk theme whose drive is not up yet, the greeting stays on screen (up to 6 s after init) so the built-in theme no longer shows for a moment before the saved one replaces it. A missing theme drive makes that boot up to 6 s longer. From RIPPS2 build 125 (akilluminati47). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* In-Game Menu (beta), RetroAchievements builds: an Achievements page, from RIPPS2 build 94 (akilluminati47). It shows how many of the game's achievements are unlocked and how many are left, and Left To Hunt lists the locked ones one at a time with their points and how to earn them. The menu shows the list as the loader last saw it: opening a game's View achievements page in xeRAbora mode now also saves the set as RA/<game ID>.ach, and the next launch takes it into the menu (up to 8 KB, placed only with In-Game Menu on). The Achievements code is built only into the RA builds; it adds nothing to the other builds' ee_core. Host-tested, builds passed; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* In-Game Menu (beta) in the RetroAchievements builds too: there ee_core has no room for it beside RA, so the menu (with the silent pause and the exact picture) is built as igrovl.elf, a 16 KB overlay the loader copies to the top of the module area (0xCC000) only for a launch with In-Game Menu on. With the menu off nothing is copied and the launch is unchanged. Games whose modules sit elsewhere, or run past 0xCC000, keep the plain combo. RETROACHIEVEMENTS=1 build passed; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* In-Game Menu (beta): the pause is now silent and gives back the exact picture, from RIPPS2 build 108 (akilluminati47). While the menu is open the game's sound stops (SPU2 volume down, every voice held) and goes on where it stopped on Resume; the pixels under the panel are kept in IOP memory and drawn back before the game runs again, so a still screen no longer keeps the panel. A game that streams PCM straight to the sound cores keeps that stream running, silently, so it does not resume from the paused spot. Both run in a new small IOP module, igrmbox.irx, packed and loaded only for a launch with In-Game Menu on: with the menu off the modules and memory a game sees are unchanged (CDVDMAN is byte-for-byte the same). A game with too little free IOP memory keeps the old behaviour. PS2SDK build passed; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* In-Game Menu (beta), from RIPPS2 (akilluminati47): with Settings > Game Launching > In-Game Menu (Beta) on (default Off), the IGR combo pauses an OPL-core game under a panel with Resume, Cheats, Exit Game and Power Off instead of leaving it. Cheats is new: every cheat of the game's file can be turned on or off while playing, applied on Resume (off stops a cheat writing, it does not undo what it wrote; the master code is always in). The menu draws into the game's own frame through GSM's write tracker, so PCSX2 and games it cannot draw on keep the plain combo. Not in RetroAchievements, IGS (EXTRA_FEATURES) or freeze-report (INGAMEDIAG) builds (no room in ee_core); the menu builds link ee_core with --gc-sections to make room. make IGR_MENU=0 leaves it out. Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Display: the 720p and 1080i video modes are now always drawn as 16:9 (they are 16:9 screens), so menus, covers and themes no longer look stretched sideways there when Widescreen is off; a theme's _hd layout applies in those modes too. Raised by KrahJohlito and Berion. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Themes: a theme without views= now offers every view (List, Coverflow, PSBBN Flow, Grid). A view the theme does not declare is built from its own layout, keeping its background, colours, fonts, icons, hints and info page and taking only the presenter (and the list position) from the built-in <OPL> theme's file for that view. views= still limits a theme to the views it names. Design: KrahJohlito (multi-view themes). Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Themes: one conf_theme.cfg can hold a 4:3 and a 16:9 layout. Any key may carry an _hd variant (used while Widescreen is on) or an _sd variant (while it is off); without one the plain key is used, so existing themes look the same. The uOPL/wOPL wsX element key is read as x_hd. Opt-in hd_autofit=1 keeps a 4:3 layout's proportions in 16:9 by scaling positions 3/4 about the screen centre. Changing Widescreen reloads only themes that use these keys. Ideas: KrahJohlito (wsX, uOPL/wOPL) and Berion (_sd/_hd with fallback). Host-tested; NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Disc key reads: release the synchronous N-command lock on success and RPC failure; repeated Load From Disc and the Launch Disc key path share the fix. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL 7f1018e7. Host-tested; hardware validation pending.
* Bound OSD history executable filenames to the 15 characters a history record stores, preventing long alternate startup names from overflowing the launch stack and letting a repeat launch find its existing record. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL 80c5558d. Host-tested; hardware validation pending.
* Keep the final NUL when fitting wrapped theme text and stop at the string boundary, preventing reads/writes beyond exact-size allocations. Existing private copies keep saved CFG text unchanged. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL a4c0830f. Hardware validation pending.
* Stop parsing at the cheat-table capacity, preserving every accepted cheat's codes.
  Credit: belomaxorka / YAOPL 44a003bd5868539481baf3c09922660246ca96f5.
* Fragmented native BDM VMC warnings show the existing fragment count and, on Cancel, backup/recovery guidance. Native refusal and physical-card fallback are unchanged. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL c19eed08. Hardware validation pending.
* Reject a SYSTEM.CNF BOOT2 line without '=' instead of passing NULL to the value parser during image discovery. Matches the existing C++ guard. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL 43781768. Hardware validation pending.
* SMB games: a read whose reply the server cuts off mid-message (for example Samba dropping an idle PS2) now fails instead of freezing the game with the SMB lock held. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL e16e2d15. Host-tested; hardware validation pending.
* IGR and power-off stop the USB host controller before the IOP reset, so IGR with a USB PADEMU pad (DualShock 3) or a USB device no longer hangs before the next program. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL e72c9f48. Host-tested; hardware validation pending.
* MMCE Game ID: an SD2PSX that stops answering while it swaps cards is waited out (bounded at 7.5 s) instead of ending the wait, so the game no longer starts while its memory card is still switching. Cards without a busy query still launch at once. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL 19578cc6 and akilluminati47 (RIPPS2) for the wait it extends. Host-tested; hardware validation pending.
* DS3/DS4 on USB: each pad now has its own report buffer and completion, a report transfer that timed out is waited out instead of being overwritten by the next one, and the DS3 enable report no longer shares the rumble/LED buffer. The 200 ms transfer timeout is now actually cancelled (it was cancelled with the wrong argument, so it fired later and woke the next transfer early); this also fixes the menu driver. Ported from belomaxorka / YAOPL (1ef5b49c, 4b1106e4, c4a82e95). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* Launching a game or ELF now hands a DualShock over as it powers up: pressure mode off, digital, unlocked, as a disc started from the OSD finds it. The menu had left it locked in DualShock mode with pressure on, and Gran Turismo 4 now and then could not take the pad over until it was replugged. Each request is waited out, bounded at 1 s; empty ports and non-DualShock pads are closed as before. Ported from belomaxorka / YAOPL (c56a91b6), which also lists upstream OPL issue #1724 as possibly the same problem. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* ISO 9660 directory walk (game list and in-game CDVDMAN): a directory record without a name no longer stops the scan (it looped forever), the record length is read as one byte (a non-zero extended-attribute byte made it step 256+ bytes or backwards), and a damaged record that is shorter than its name or runs past the sector ends that sector instead of being read past. The found file name is cut to 16 bytes and taken after either / or \ in both copies, the game list compares names within the record (odd-length names were missed), and the in-game directory read stays inside its sector. Ported from belomaxorka / YAOPL (ff498c19, af5b52b7, bfe726f5). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* ZSO images: a header the reader cannot read (align above 11, or blocks other than 2048 bytes, which maxcso writes for images of 2 GiB and more) is no longer opened as ZSO, so it is not listed and cannot divide by zero or decode 16 KiB blocks into a 2 KiB buffer. An index whose offsets go backwards, or whose blocks are larger than the sectors they decode to, is a failed read instead of data written outside the buffer, and reads of more than 256 sectors now go in slices (they used to fail every time). Ported from belomaxorka / YAOPL (0253f98b, 9ad4afeb, 147e2493, 4baf5921). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* BdmIndex shows one dot per visible mass device, in menu order: two devices show two dots (it showed five), devices in slots 0 and 2 both get dots, and a lone device shows none instead of "3 of 5". New Index2_0..Index4_3 pictures are drawn from Index_0 by tools/make_bdmindex.py; a theme with only its own five-dot pictures keeps them by slot. Ported from belomaxorka / YAOPL (f84b227d). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* MMCE Settings: the IGR Boot Card Slot(s) choices Off and Both, and the On/Off choices, now come from the language file instead of fixed English ("NONE", "BOTH", "OFF", "ON"). New language string BOTH, translated in every fork overlay; stored values are unchanged. Ported from belomaxorka / YAOPL (999bb6d3). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* In-game network: give the SMAP TX descriptor the TX buffer address (SMAP_TX_BASE + the FIFO write offset), as every other SMAP driver does, Neutrino's included; it had the bare offset. SMB games and RA telemetry send through it. Credit zokzot (xeRAbora OPL 205223e2). Not tested on hardware.
* Read-only UDPBD/UDPFS IMG servers (udpbd-vexfat, udpbd-server on a read-only image, PS2-Servers on a folder or with --read-only): OPL now writes and reads back a test file when such a device connects. On one that keeps nothing it creates no folders or games.bin cache, never saves OPL's settings there, keeps that device's game settings in CFG/ next to OPL's own (a CFG already on the server is still read), drops a VMC set for its games (they save to the real memory card), and hides Rename, Delete, VMC and Ember settings for its games and apps. The UDPBD driver counts a write the server refuses as done, so one refused write no longer makes the whole disk unreadable. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL (Roman Kelesidis) 093b541b..760d7e3c and df65546e. Host-tested; hardware validation pending.
* The screen position (H-POS, V-POS and Overscan) is now kept for each video mode, so 480i, 576i, 480p and 1080i each keep their own centring. Changing the mode brings back the position it had; the shared keys are still written, so older builds read the same values. Ported from RIPPS2 build 124 (akilluminati47). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* The menu now starts in the saved Video Mode and Widescreen setting, read from the memory-card settings file before the screen is first set, instead of starting in Auto and switching a moment later; 480p and 1080i sets and HDMI adapters resync once instead of twice. Settings on USB, the HDD or the network keep the old start. Holding START at boot still ignores the settings, and the recovery combos still apply. Ported from RIPPS2 build 120 (akilluminati47). NOT TESTED on hardware.
* RetroAchievements docs, release notes and the kit's xeRAbora.url now point at xeRAbora v1.0.1, the current stable client; alpha.17 or later works. A source review of alpha.17...v1.0.1 found no console protocol change. v1.0.1 is NOT TESTED on hardware with the RA build.
* UDPFS Files games can run on the OPL core: per game with Loader Core <OPL>, or when Neutrino cannot run them (no neutrino.elf, a .zso image). Neutrino stays the default. The menu keeps the ISO open on the server across the IOP reset and the new udpfs_fhi module reads it in game; VMCs are opened read-write on the server and saved there through the new udpfs_mcemu. NOT TESTED on hardware.
* UDPBD and UDPFS games: the disc driver stops a USB host controller the menu left running, which could hang a game at its first screen with a USB drive plugged in. Credit belomaxorka/YAOPL (Roman Kelesidis) 15eee615. NOT TESTED on hardware.

==== Version 0.9.3 ====
CORE:

* New RDB-based DECI2 Debugging System.
* Refactored and optimized core modules.
* New CDVDMAN streaming mechanism for better performance.
* Kinder, gentler, and hopefully better IGR mechanism
* Added support for the DTL-T10000, for debugging.
* Updated USB drivers - support drives greater than 1TB but less than 2TB in capacity, plus better reliability.
* Eliminated the need for user-configurable delays in USB support.
* Improved performance and stability of SMB support.
* VMC Fix - Slot2 should no longer clone Slot1 and vice versa
* Removed obsolete Compatibility Modes and needless GSM video modes.
* New PS2RD Cheat Engine port by Doctorxyz.
* Per-Game GSM Support.
* New super-slim EE core, making mode 1 (Alt EE core) obsolete.
* Added Accurate Reads mode, for emulating the reading speed and behaviour of the CD/DVD drive.
* The CallBack Timer (CBT) setting now uses a standardized value and was merged into Accurate Reads mode.
* Added a workaround for some clone network adaptors.
* Mode 7 "IOP threading hack" removed, as the new streaming mechanism has taken care of all related issues.
* New compatibility mode: "high module storage". For games that need OPL to store its modules elsewhere, to avoid a memory conflict.
* Improved reading performance of the cdrom device.
* Improved reliability of some CDVDMAN functions, for more consistent behaviour.
* Improved DVD-DL support.
* Changed "Disable DVD-DL" to "Emulate DVD-DL" to better explain what it does. It's to emulate DVD-DL support, for DVD9 rips (games with their 2 layers compacted into 1).
* Fixed support for SMB usernames and passwords that are longer than 16 characters (limit extended to 31).
* Fixed renaming functionality for USBExtreme games.
* Various fixes for games.

GUI:

* Improved the behaviour of the auto-refresh option.
* GSM moved to Game Options menu since its a Per-Game option now.
* Infamous "Blockhead Grande" theme bug SQUARSHED! (Themes should now get loaded correctly, regardless of display settings).
* New logo design by Berion, new changed icons by El_Patas.
* Better error reporting and help messages in general.
* Network settings are now saved in opl_network.cfg.
* Improved stability, design and UI responsiveness.
* Added missing icon hints.
* Fixed the problem with the HDLDump server being difficult to shut down properly.
* Fixed HDD corruption caused by deleting a game from the HDD unit.
* Added a new network update mechanism, which allows game compatibility records to be automatically downloaded from the OPL-CL service.
* SMB server can now be specified by its NetBIOS name.
* IP address configuration can be set automatically with DHCP, although it is still recommended to reserve an IP address for the PS2 in the network because the DHCP reservation will not be ever renewed while in-game.
* Renamed "Enable Delete and Rename" to "Enable Write Operations".
* Changed the delete and modify VMC controls to be disabled instead of hidden, when writes are disabled.
* ISO disc images no longer strictly need to be named in a special format. Simply put your ISO files in your CD and DVD folders and OPL will find them.
* Renamed compatibility modes to have actual names.
* Game history will now be updated; the "towers" behind the "SONY Computer Entertainment" boot screen should continue to grow.
* Added support for OTF fonts.
* Added support for fonts stored on the HDD unit (root of +OPL partition; hdd0:+OPL/) and USB device (root of device; mass0:/).

GAME FIXES & COMPATIBILITY IMPROVEMENTS:
* New patch: Choujikuu Yousai Macross
* New patch: Super Robot Wars IMPACT
* Drive state of sceCdStandby has been changed to PAUSE: Check iTV
* New patch: Ratchet and Clank: Up Your Arsenal
* New patch: The Oneechanbara
* New patch: The Oneechanpuruu
* New streaming mechanism for better playability: Various BEMANI games
* Initialization is performed for search functions: Lifeline

==== Version 0.9.2 ====
rev672

CORE:

* Merged OPL/OPLGSM codebase
* GSM Core 0.36.R - don't worry; 0.38 will be coming back better than ever!
* GSM Core no longer supports 576p, 1080p, Skip FMVs - this is temporary.
* GSM Core is now IGR and CodeBreaker/PS2rd compatible!
* GSM no longer included in Childproof builds.
* Unified Makefile builds from single source tree via "GSM=0/1" argument (ala VMC/No VMC)
* The integrated LibFreeType was removed, upgraded, and moved into the PS2SDK
* Upgraded LIBPNG, ATAD, HDPro, and DEV9 Module Code
* Added code for the power-off RPC, for older games. They should be compatible now.
* Added power-off processing code. Games should be able to power-off the console now.
* Optimzed CDVDMAN and CDVDFSV
* Support for PSX (DVR) units
* Built-in TLB reinitialization mechanism - no more EECORE hooking and patching.
* Added compatibility mode 7 - "IOP Threading Hack".
* Replaced SMAP driver.
* Modified SMSTCPIP.
* Ported a version of ETH Mode types from doctorxyz's OPLGSM.
* Retired the built-in kernel update for Protokernel consoles (SCPH-10000 and SCPH-15000).

GUI:

* New "Show GSM on Main Menu" toggle in "Settings" (GSM Builds Only)
* New "GSM Settings" on Main Menu - easier navigation! (GSM Builds Only)
* Fixed issue with HDLSERV and GSM Settings not showing up immediately.
* Full Ethernet controls - can disable Auto-Negotiation and force a mode.
* Some things were are worded differently as less words carry more freight.
* Removed redundant UDMA modes - PS2 will never handle UDMA 5 and UDMA 6.
* Updated SMB support to give better error messages.
* Network error codes changed slightly - 300 for connection errors, 301 for logon errors, 302 for ECHO isalive
  test failing, and 303 for share opening errors.


COMPATIBILITY:

* Kingdom Hearts 2 Final Mix (Gummi Fix)
* Baldar's Gate Series (HDD)
* Champions of Norrath (HDD)
* New Mode 7 fixes stuttering with games such as DDR and Pop'N Music (HDD ONLY!)

